<ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">pack</ansi>

Each character has one Pack equipment slot. Your cloth knapsack provides 10 kg
of shared cargo space. Recruits bring a starter knapsack too. Assigned packs on
living, present carriers add capacity; fallen or away carriers add none.
Horses add their eligible capacity. There is no base or Strength cargo allowance.

  company equip [member] [exact-item-reference]
  Assign a pack from shared cargo.
  company remove [member] pack
  Return that exact pack to shared cargo.
  company compare [member] [exact-item-reference]
  Preview cargo and capacity changes.
  company inventory
  See container availability and the single shared item list.

Satchels provide 5 kg, traveller's packs 10 kg, and frame packs 15 kg.
Spare packs provide no capacity and count as cargo weight. Assigned pack tare
does not consume its usable capacity. Packs and their contents are dropped for
combat; they add no combat burden.

Losing capacity never deletes cargo. An overloaded company can walk, sell,
drop or consume cargo, remove packs, or assign a larger pack to recover.
Ordinary additions and gear changes that worsen an excess are refused.
At full load, travel takes 50% longer and walking fatigue increases 30%.

Older saves assign existing suitable packs once, then grant a starter to each
member lacking one. All exact items are kept; excess cargo remains overloaded.
A spent starter grant never repeats on login, removal or resurrection.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help equipment</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help burden</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help mount</ansi>.
